s=s.replace('## Evidence standards replacing the confidence score','## Account and tax structure\n\nThe original Irish-fund suggestion needs qualification. For a qualifying nonresident noncitizen, $60,000 is generally an aggregate US-situs estate filing threshold, not a per-account allowance or a flat 40% tax calculation. UAE residence alone does not establish US citizenship, tax residence or estate domicile. Irish corporate fund shares generally reduce the direct US-share situs issue; US stocks in other accounts still count. [IRS estate guidance](https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/frequently-asked-questions-on-estate-taxes-for-nonresidents-not-citizens-of-the-united-states).\n\nEligible Irish funds generally incur 15% US portfolio-dividend withholding at fund level. That is different from the usual 30% direct-dividend withholding for a qualifying nonresident individual without treaty relief. Accumulation reinvests net dividends; it is not tax-free treatment. [US–Ireland treaty](https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-trty/ireland.pdf), [IRS Publication 519](https://www.irs.gov/publications/p519).\n\nIssuer checks identify CSPX (IE00B5BMR087) and VUAA (IE00BFMXXD54) as Irish accumulating S&P 500 UCITS share classes with published 0.07% ongoing fees and London USD listings. Product identity is verified; suitability, account eligibility, fraction availability, live spread and exact contract are not. [iShares issuer page](https://www.ishares.com/uk/individual/en/products/253743/ishares-sp-500-b-ucits-etf-acc-fund), [Vanguard issuer page](https://www.vanguard.co.uk/professional/product/etf/equity/9694/sp-500-ucits-etf-).\n\n## Evidence standards replacing the confidence score')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('review/WEEKLY_INVESTMENT_POLICY.md');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig').replace('at most 2% per stock; at most 5% per sector in the individual-stock sleeve','at most 2% of total mandate capital per directly held stock; at most 5% of total mandate capital per sector in the individual-stock sleeve')
s=s.replace('- Count overlapping index holdings','- Risk denominator is provisionally the $50,000–$100,000 mandate capital; household suitability is not established. Report mandate-only and aggregate exposure including separate algorithmic trading. The proposed ceiling is not an instruction to liquidate unknown existing holdings.\n- Direct-stock caps apply to the direct sleeve; separately report combined issuer/sector exposures through funds. Count overlapping index holdings')
s=s.replace('- Stop orders can fill worse','- Data-provider failure freezes new discretionary buys; it does not automatically require liquidation of existing positions. Report failed/stale inputs explicitly.\n- Define one-way weekly turnover as 0.5 × (gross purchases + gross sales) / opening NAV, with contributions and withdrawals separately reported.\n- Stop orders can fill worse')
